# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# ESP32-P4 with external PSRAM.
#
# The global beatgrid needs 807,296 bytes of workspace. Measured on a P4 v1.3
# board with internal RAM only, 606,484 bytes were free and requesting it failed
# with APTA_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY before the first block was accepted. The S6 bin
# ring accounts for roughly 624 KB of that on its own.
#
# With these settings the same board reports 32 MB of PSRAM and every feature
# set runs. It is not free: the S6 workspace no longer fits in internal SRAM, so
# it lands in PSRAM, and the global-grid rows cost about 3.5 times more relative
# to the host than the rows whose working set stays internal. See section 29 of
# the S4 status document.
#
# Use alongside sdkconfig.defaults:
#
#   idf.py -B build-esp32p4 \
#     -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.p4.defaults" \
#     set-target esp32p4 build
#
# ESP-IDF 6.0.2 builds P4 firmware requiring chip revision v3.1 or newer. A
# v1.x board needs 5.5, which supports v0.0 through v1.0.
CONFIG_SPIRAM=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_HEX=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_SPEED_20M=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_USE_MALLOC=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_TRY_ALLOCATE_WIFI_LWIP=y
